### Part 2: What Kind of Questions Should You Demo?

When you fire up the web dashboard (`http://192.168.4.1`) or test it locally in `sim.py`, you want to show off that your microcontrollers aren't just matching keywords—they are tracking **space, time, objects, and pronouns**. 

Here is a curated menu of impressive prompts to copy-paste for a demo:

#### 1. Multi-Hop Object Tracking (The Classic bAbI Test)
*Proves the model understands object permanence and movement handoffs.*
> **Prompt:** `[c] alice found the ball in the room . then alice went to the garden . [q] where is the ball ? [a]`
> **Expected Output:** `garden .`

#### 2. Chain of Custody / Entity Transfers
*Proves it can track who currently holds an item across multiple handoffs.*
> **Prompt:** `[c] bob gave the cup to alice . then alice gave the cup to luna . [q] who has the cup now ? [a]`
> **Expected Output:** `luna .`

#### 3. Pronoun Coreference Resolution
*Proves it can map a pronoun ("she"/"he") back to the correct named character.*
> **Prompt:** `[c] luna was in the kitchen . then she went to the room . [q] where is luna ? [a]`
> **Expected Output:** `room .`

#### 4. Spatial Negation
*Proves it handles negative constraints and resolves to the alternative truth.*
> **Prompt:** `[c] bob is not in the kitchen . bob is in the park . [q] where is bob ? [a]`
> **Expected Output:** `park .`

#### 5. Compass / Relational Mapping
*Proves it understands abstract 2D grid relationships.*
> **Prompt:** `[c] the kitchen is north of the park . the park is north of the room . [q] what is north of the park ? [a]`
> **Expected Output:** `kitchen .`

#### 6. Time Reasoning (Before/After)
*Proves it can look backward chronologically through a timeline.*
> **Prompt:** `[c] first bob was in the room . then bob was in the kitchen . [q] where was bob first ? [a]`
> **Expected Output:** `room .`

#### 7. The Mode Switch (Open-Ended Storytelling)
*Proves that when you strip away the logic tags, it transforms back into a creative neural net.*
> **Prompt:** `once upon a time alice and luna went into the green garden and`
> **Expected Output:** *(It will fluently continue writing a fairy tale using its TinyStories background training).*